Z||000005||Formula88||05-30-2001||06:33 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by TSPalmer:<BR><B>She got it fixed by dropping the fuel tank and found a rotten rubber hose.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>YES!!!!  I do so love it when what appears to be a hugh disaster turns out to be an easy fix.  My Formula died on me in Greensboro once. All I could figure was it wasn't getting gas. After a tow home and 2 weeks of diags in my spare time, it turned out to be a faulty wire to the ECM!  Total repair cost - nada - cuz I had some wire and electrical tape at home.  And I thought I'd have to pull the gas tank... <P>Oh, and thanks again to the people on the Forum who helped me diag that problem!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||84Bill||05-30-2001||07:05 PM||||Had a similar situation when the previous owner saw coolant spewing out of a pipe in the engine compartment. Well after pitting 1300 bucks in parts in this car then searching for this part and never finding it he sold it to me for 600 bucks. I knew all along what it was. It was the heater hose on the water pump, it had a hole in it and when coolant shot out of the hose it ran right up the side of the A/C line and it appeared to be leaking coolant from the A/C hose thus the part was impossible to find since it is not related to the cooling system. Well after cutting off the effected area I had not further problems except for an ignition module.||||reg||14
Z||000007||grinthock||05-30-2001||07:24 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 84Bill:<BR><B>Had a similar situation when the previous owner saw coolant spewing out of a pipe in the engine compartment. Well after pitting 1300 bucks in parts in this car then searching for this part and never finding it he sold it to me for 600 bucks. I knew all along what it was. It was the heater hose on the water pump, it had a hole in it and when coolant shot out of the hose it ran right up the side of the A/C line and it appeared to be leaking coolant from the A/C hose thus the part was impossible to find since it is not related to the cooling system. Well after cutting off the effected area I had not further problems except for an ignition module.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Yep and the ignition module probably got fried by the coolant all over it<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||maryjane||05-30-2001||09:00 PM||||I'm glad to hear she got it running, hope she goes ahead and makes a great car out of it. She sure had her troubles for a while there. One question . How could the fuel line relate to all that oil burned in such ashort trip? At least it will run, a LOT easier to troubleshoot one that will start, than not.<BR>Don||||reg||7
